<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharif ul-Hashim of Sulu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Sayyid Abu Bakr, Sharif ul-Hashim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharif ul-Hashim, also called Sayyid Abu Bakr, is credited in Sulu tradition as the founder and first sultan of the Sulu Sultanate in the mid-fifteenth century. Said in the Sulu genealogies to be an Arab scholar who came by way of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a>, he married the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-baguinda">Rajah Baguinda</a>, took the title of sultan and organised the state on Islamic lines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharif-ul-hashim-of-sulu.jpg" alt="Sharif ul-Hashim of Sulu" width="177" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sayyid_Abubakr_bin_Shaikh_Al-Kaff_(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
